Take a moment to appreciate who is publicly calling for the CLARITY Act to pass:

@realDonaldTrump - the US President
@SecScottBessent - Treasury Secretary
@SenLummis - US Senator
@SenatorTimScott - Senate Banking Chairman
@berniemoreno - US Senator
@SenKevinCramer - US Senator
@GOPMajorityWhip - House Majority Whip
@RepFrenchHill - House Financial Services Chairman
@RepBryanSteil - Digital Assets Subcommittee Chairman
@RepMeuser - US Congressman
@RepStutzman - US Congressman
@DavidSacks - White House AI & Crypto Czar

These are some of the most powerful people on the planet. All on record, all calling for pro-crypto legislation.

And that’s just the politicians. Add the biggest institutions in finance to the mix: BlackRock, Fidelity, Goldman Sachs, JP Morgan, Franklin Templeton, you name it.

Five years ago crypto was a shady topic politicians and institutions wouldn’t touch. Today the most influential people and companies in the world are going on record to say this industry needs a clear framework to thrive.

Let that sink in for a second, because the shift itself is bigger than any single bill could ever be.

Sure, we all want the CLARITY Act to pass, and sooner or later it will anyway. But the fact that the most powerful politicians and institutions on earth are now openly debating how to support this industry, not whether to, tells you everything.

The whole world has realized crypto is here to stay.

We already won.

